{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "03Q4", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0002": "$X_{affine, \\etale}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{topologies-lemma-alternative}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-colimit-affine-sites}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{sites-cohomology-lemma-colimit}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9b4dc44db025ccf48455c531f6cadc77d7455dbf39d9667eecc05cb640280a48", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:46333de33ab29a87a6f0bf5e6fca6f0b425ba6d1e86b3583f783c925f696b5d3", "source_text": "By Topologies, Lemma <REF_0001>\nwe can compute the cohomology\nof <MATH_0001> on <MATH_0002>.\nThus the result by a combination of\nLemma <REF_0002>\nand\nCohomology on Sites, Lemma <REF_0003>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:1d2ae1dde2b9a9634674227ccdc0c9adc715314d94bca4c016ab175bc7ede3de", "unit_id": "tag:09YQ:proof"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "03Q4", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9a67df96346e5bad4a59b66b2486ff51a998f011ff0637037b3894e001dd797c", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe following two results are special cases of the theorem above.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4b984e46fe2eda9cbe61d75724dbc545b2b5252666c2d638187e72ce0c4f6aaa", "unit_id": "tag:03Q4:prose-0004"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "03Q4", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$I$", "MATH_0003": "$(\\mathcal{F}_i, \\varphi_{ij})$", "MATH_0004": "$X_\\etale$", "MATH_0005": "$I$", "MATH_0006": "$$\n\\colim_{i\\in I} H_\\etale^p(X, \\mathcal{F}_i) = H_\\etale^p(X,\n\\colim_{i\\in I} \\mathcal{F}_i).\n$$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-colimit}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:dd31939b2cc4e817b48fd6b7d5fa606e8a12d4b301fe9d3b6f7eb9e88b535bca", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b7cd33d10acc4ae4c01f3b493c776802f99ac4c80b5ceaa29c53edbb4fb98318", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a quasi-compact and quasi-separated scheme. Let <MATH_0002>\nbe a directed set. Let <MATH_0003> be a system\nof abelian sheaves on <MATH_0004> over <MATH_0005>. Then\n<MATH_0006>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5a3cad1f581dae8d7f12ec0e6edb29ada491a05ba9f17a05fc13ef03468f3740", "unit_id": "tag:03Q5:statement"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "03Q4", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\v C", "GROUPCLOSE_0001": "}", "GROUPOPEN_0001": "{", "MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$p$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{U}$", "MATH_0005": "$X$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{V} = \\{V_j \\to X\\}_{j\\in J}$", "MATH_0007": "$J$", "MATH_0008": "$V_j$", "MATH_0009": "$V_{j_0} \\times_X \\ldots \\times_X V_{j_p}$", "MATH_0010": "$p = 0$", "MATH_0011": "$X$", "MATH_0012": "$V_{j_0} \\times_X \\ldots \\times_X V_{j_p}$", "MATH_0013": "$p \\to p + 1$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{theorem-colimit}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-locality-cohomology}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{theorem-cech-ss}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:51da2cde285391bd0813abbc0755a1e04a31491b85c957da28b0b8c7ad302d28", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:fb11208e30bd8c43bdbd3e541c473d3011279c726374d134eeb04663920863fb", "source_text": "This is a special case of Theorem <REF_0001>.\nWe also sketch a direct proof.\nWe prove it for all <MATH_0001> at the same time, by induction on <MATH_0002>.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002>\nFor any quasi-compact and quasi-separated scheme <MATH_0003> and any <ACCENT_0001>tale covering\n<MATH_0004> of <MATH_0005>, show that there exists a refinement\n<MATH_0006> with <MATH_0007> finite and each <MATH_0008>\nquasi-compact and quasi-separated such that all\n<MATH_0009> are also\nquasi-compact and quasi-separated.\n<STRUCT_0003>\nUsing the previous step and the definition of colimits in the category of\nsheaves, show that the theorem holds for <MATH_0010> and all <MATH_0011>.\n<STRUCT_0004>\nUsing the locality of cohomology\n(Lemma <REF_0002>),\nthe <GROUPOPEN_0001><ACCENT_0002><GROUPCLOSE_0001>ech-to-cohomology spectral sequence\n(Theorem <REF_0003>) and the fact that the induction\nhypothesis applies to all\n<MATH_0012>\nin the above situation, prove the induction step <MATH_0013>.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:16bf383187fec4b7e0b7e35d3fb1aa7a2e06b5f23ca088f02bcdff4b9b1b0fa0", "unit_id": "tag:03Q5:proof"}
